y of its own to re-store, so its entry is refreshed on sight instead. `run.reuse_pr_summaries` (boolean, default true) restores the old behaviour; it is declared in `config.schema.json` because `run` is `additionalProperties: false`, where an undeclared key read by the runner does not degrade but aborts the host's nightly at config validation — so the config case is tested through `load_config_validated`, not a raw dict. The saving is reported as an `info_only` `pr_summaries_reused: n/m` reason: it describes work the run did NOT have to do, the opposite of a degradation, and flipping `partial` on a successful saving would cost auto-merge every night through CCE-140's `partial and not advance_cursor_backed` gate — turning the optimization into an outage. It is recorded at all because a saving nobody can see is indistinguishable from a feature that silently stopped working.
 
